WEB SOURCE (the specification) — components/forms/CurrencyInput.tsx (+ lib/currencyFormat.ts)
  CurrencyInput.tsx — a controlled, currency-aware number field built on <Input>:
    • Stores its value in integer MICRO-units (1 major unit = 1_000_000) so currencies with 0/2/3/4 fractional
      digits round-trip without floating-point loss (valueToMicro / microToValue).
    • Renders the value via Intl.NumberFormat style:'currency' (symbol/position/decimal per locale: "$1.50" vs
      "1,50 €" vs "£1.50") with useGrouping:false for the editable field; nil/non-finite -> "".
    • Shows the localized currency symbol as a leading aria-hidden icon adornment (currencySymbol).
    • Parses typed text on blur / Enter: strips the localized symbol on either side, the literal ISO code
      ("USD 1.50"), locale group separators ("1,234.56" / "1.234,56" / "1 234,56"), accounting parentheses for
      negatives ("($1.50)" -> -1.5); commits the canonical micro then renormalises the display.
    • Focus guard: re-syncs the local text buffer from the parent's valueMicro ONLY when the field is NOT focused,
      so an external change never clobbers in-progress typing. inputMode=decimal, autoComplete=off, aria-label.
  lib/currencyFormat.ts — valueToMicro/microToValue (MICRO_SCALE 1e6, Math.round), formatCurrencyValue/Micro
    (Intl currency, clampPrecision [0,20] default 2, code-prefixed fallback on RangeError), currencySymbol
    (formatToParts), currencyCodeFromSymbol (symbol->ISO table), parseCurrencyText/ToMicro, parseLocaleNumber
    (locale group/decimal separators; space-like group separators stripped).
  i18n keys extracted from source — the documented canonical ariaLabel "Electricity Cost (per kWh)".

