NAMING NOTE (logged; no silent drift)
  The sibling Currency display surface (0083) already declares a module-public `CurrencyInput` value type (its input
  snapshot) plus a `Currency*` core. Two same-named module-public types cannot coexist, and Currency.* is OUT of my
  allowed glob. So the view is named `CurrencyInputField` and every symbol is namespaced `CurrencyInputField*`; the
  diagnostics slug + the web parity intent stay "CurrencyInput" (CurrencyInputFieldMeta.surfaceSlug).

PARITY MAPPING (web -> Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  <Input value/onChange (controlled)   -> P1/S8 CurrencyInputFieldSource (Live/InMemory) -> ...Model; the view does
                                          no HTTP. commit(_:) carries the parsed micro back (the web onChange).
  valueToMicro / microToValue          -> CurrencyInputFieldMicro (1e6 scale, rounded; nil/non-finite -> nil).
  formatCurrencyMicro (Intl currency)  -> CurrencyInputFieldFormatter.format (NumberFormatter .currency, useGrouping
                                          false, .halfUp to match Intl halfExpand; code-prefixed fallback).
  currencySymbol                       -> Formatter.symbol (NumberFormatter.currencySymbol; literal-code fallback).
  currencyCodeFromSymbol               -> Formatter.code(fromSymbol:) table (default USD).
  parseCurrencyText / parseLocaleNumber-> Formatter.parse / parseLocaleNumber (symbol+ISO strip, parens, leading
                                          sign, locale group/decimal seps incl. space-like U+00A0/U+202F).
  local text + focusedRef guard        -> Model.editingText + beginEditing/commitEditing/submit; apply() re-syncs the
                                          buffer to the canonical display ONLY when not editing (verbatim web guard).
  symbol icon adornment (aria-hidden)  -> leading muted symbol glyph, accessibilityHidden; field carries aria-label.
  render (no loading/empty/error)      -> the editable field is the `ready` phase; the P4 leaf states (loading /
                                          error / stale / offline) are added as native chrome so it is never a blank
                                          box. The blank value renders as an empty, usable field + a "not set" hint.
  i18n                                 -> every string via CurrencyInputFieldStrings (P1/S10); English fallbacks.
  telemetry                            -> view.opened surface="CurrencyInput" once on appear (P1/S11).
  Reduce Motion                        -> TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton honour accessibilityReduceMotion.

  Parity decisions (logged, no silent drift):
    • NumberFormatter defaults to banker's (half-even) rounding; Intl.NumberFormat rounds half away from zero
      (halfExpand). Pinned `.halfUp` so 123_450 micro @ precision 4 -> "$0.1235" (not "$0.1234"), matching the web
      test. Asserted by testRespectsPrecisionForDisplayRounding.
    • The web `parseLocaleNumber` strips space + U+00A0 group separators; today's ICU uses U+202F (narrow no-break
      space) for fr-FR, so the native strips all three space-like separators — the web's intent, generalised.
    • An unresolvable ISO code: NumberFormatter renders the code itself ("ZZZ 1.50", non-breaking space), which is
      the web's code-prefixed fallback shape; a defensive plain-decimal fallback covers the empty/`¤`-symbol case.
    • The web shows the symbol BOTH as the aria-hidden icon AND inside the formatted value; reproduced faithfully
      (leading muted glyph + the canonical formatted text).

STATES (every web behaviour + P4 leaf state reproduced — never a hidden/blank surface)
  loading   : skeleton label + field-shaped block (the bound value's fetch in flight).
  ready      (empty)     : the editable field with the symbol adornment, blank value, + a "not set" hint.
  ready      (populated) : the editable field showing the canonical formatted value ("$1.50" / "1,50 €" / "£1.50").
  error     : retry tile (web QueryError peer — the parent settings fetch failed).
  stale     : freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the rising edge.
  offline   : freshness chip over the cached value (no auto-refresh while offline).
  Each state has a #if DEBUG preview + a unit test.

